    "counters": [],
    "adapt": "A collective-farm fuel yard: the barn is the host (yard on its -z side). Fuel tanks and a pump stand on the -x side of the yard, the tanker is parked nose along it on the +x side, drums and pallets lie by the barn front, an attendant hut and a price board by the gate, and a net-fence ring with an 8 m gate gap closes the yard. The kit has no front: a long barn has an entrance far to one side, so the quarter-turn rule would turn the yard onto the barn end; the yard keeps the barn yaw (the yard lies on the -z side, the barn back, where the open dirt yard is). Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch. The `depot-load` barrel (LF_FuelDepot: LF_FuelDepotComponent plus \"Load the tanker\", #3330) stands 4 m from the tanker's origin, inside the 12 m reach of the haul."
